  "description": "When the daemon that runs for good checks the disks' mounts, runs a pass, and how long it sleeps. A check is due once check_due_ns has come. A pass is due for each reason that holds, in this order: start (no pass since it started, first), reload (the configuration was read again, reloaded), gone (a disk went missing), back (a disk came back), events (a group ripened that someone other than Atoll made: ripe_origins holds anything but atoll), due (pass_due_ns, the last pass's next_due, has come), rescan (rescan_every_ns has gone by since last_pass_end_ns, and now is inside the window, in timezone). wake_ns is the earliest of: the next check, pass_due_ns, group_due_ns (when a waiting group ripens), and the next rescan, the first time inside the window at or after last_pass_end_ns + rescan_every_ns; never before now. With hash_pending, files may wait for their hash: read_hashes is true inside the window, after any check and pass due, and outside it the window's next start is one more time to wake at. With scrub_pending, copies may be due for the scrub: inside scrub_window, scrub_opened_ns is when that stretch of it began; scrub is true when scrub_spent_ns, the budget spent in the stretch that began at scrub_spent_opened_ns, is less than scrub_budget_ns, counting as nothing a budget spent in another stretch, and no hashes are to be read first. When the budget is spent, the next stretch's start is one more time to wake at; outside the window, its next start. With backup_pending, the stretch of window that holds now, or the next one, has no catalog backup yet: backup is true inside the window when no hash is to be read first, and comes before the scrub; outside it, the window's next start is one more time to wake at. With changed_pending, a pass left files whose changed copies must be read to be decided: read_changed is true, inside the window or not, after any check and pass due and before every other step. With after_pass, the last step the daemon took was a pass, a check aside: when read_changed, notify, smart, balance, read_hashes, backup or scrub is true and every reason that holds is events or due, because is empty, as that step runs first, the reasons kept for the turn after it; a pass for any other reason does not wait.",
